Z||000001||artherd||09-02-2001||01:29 AM||||Posting this from my 500mhz pismo (looks the same as yours, but has builtin firewire ports.)  I belive if the keyboard is bronze, it should have the DVD drive.<P>To tell for sure, pull the drive module, and *flip it over* and on the bottom it will say "apple DVD drive" or not  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>PS: a good site for portable macs: <A HREF="http://www.pbzone.com" TARGET=_blank>www.pbzone.com</A>  all kinds of usefull stuff there!<P>Best!!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroSTETZ:<BR><B>recently got a 333 g3 powerbook g3 series (bronze keyboard) 10gb travelstar, 192mb ram, etc etc- i saw on everymac.com that that laptop cant handle dvd-anyone know if that is accurate? anyone have a dvd for one for sale? need some input, i would love to have the fiero powered by apple if possible, but want to use a dvd powered computer<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
