Z||000004||beer_stud_21||09-02-2001||05:50 AM||||Hey, more mac fold... thats cool!  FieroSTETZ what you have there is refered to as a Lombard Powerbook G3.  Off the top of my head im pretty sure it used software DVD decoding so yes- you can go on ebay and pick up a DVD expansion bay drive.  Then you need to get the apple DVD player software.  Either version 2.2 for OS 9.0.4 and below or version 2.4 if your running 9.1  If your not already you really should upgrade to 9.0.4 and 9.1 if you want.  <P>If any of you mac fieroers want to add me to your icq list my # is 8273989.  Im happy to answer yer mac questions.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||09-04-2001||02:57 AM||||Her marlin, macs are fun !<BR>(and man, airport/wavelan just rules  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I am pretty sure the pre-pismos (Lombards) are hardware dvd decode... BUT I belive they all have the chipset, so you can still slap an drive in and go.<P>I agree, OS9.1 is a must.  Here's a tip, if you buy OSX&lt;$99bux&gt;, you get an 9.1 CD in the box too  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
